Usage: SET COLORIZE_NICKS [ON|OFF|TOGGLE]
  When ON (the default), every nickname the client displays is
  shown in a colour picked deterministically from the nickname
  itself. A given nick always gets the same colour, so the same
  person looks the same in messages, joins, parts, NAMES, WHO and
  the status bar. The colour is computed from a hash of the nick
  (case is ignored), so no two sessions and no two windows ever
  disagree.

  The colours are drawn from a fixed palette chosen for legibility
  on dark terminals. Colouring only wraps the nick
  itself; mIRC colour codes in message text are left untouched.

  Colours are only visible when SET DISPLAY_ANSI is ON; with ANSI
  display OFF the colour codes are stripped and nicks show plain.

  Use SET COLORIZE_WARP to shift the whole colour assignment if you
  do not like the colour a particular nick was given.

See Also:
  SET COLORIZE_CHANNELS
  SET COLORIZE_WARP
  SET DISPLAY_ANSI
